{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgENJh7JyVLgTtdwgX6N6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EXo9ssLEdf8Yq6Dv2Gf1nZ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-TycjY9; python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('server.py').read()\ndef r(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s; s=s.replace(a,b,1)\nr('''    expires_in = int(tok.get(\"expires_in\") or DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL)\n    refresh = tok.get(\"refresh_token\")\n    if not refresh:\n        log(f\"{user_id}: no refresh_token in response, scheduling expiry in {expires_in}s\")\n''','''    # Intervals tokens do not expire and come without refresh_token/expires_in;\n    # they are valid until the athlete revokes them (detected lazily on a 401).\n    expires_in = int(tok[\"expires_in\"]) if tok.get(\"expires_in\") else None\n    refresh = tok.get(\"refresh_token\")\n''')\nr('\"expires_at\": time.time() + expires_in,','\"expires_at\": time.time() + expires_in if expires_in else None,')\nr('(expires in {expires_in}s)\")','(expires in {expires_in or \"never\"})\")')\nr('''c[\"status\"] != \"connected\" or c[\"expires_at\"] - now > 300:''','''c[\"status\"] != \"connected\" or c[\"expires_at\"] is None or c[\"expires_at\"] - now > 300:''')\nr('''        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/auth/init\":\n            return self.auth_init()\n''','')\nr('''    def do_POST(self):\n        url = urllib.parse.urlsplit(self.path)\n''','''    def do_POST(self):\n        url = urllib.parse.urlsplit(self.path)\n        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/auth/init\":\n            return self.auth_init()\n''')\nr('self.redirect(AUTHORIZE_URL + \"?\" + urllib.parse.urlencode(params, safe=\":,\"))','self.send_json(200, {\"authorize_url\": AUTHORIZE_URL + \"?\" + urllib.parse.urlencode(params, safe=\":,\")})')\nr('''    # Step 1: build the authorize URL and send the browser to Intervals.''','''    # Step 1: build the authorize URL; the SPA (fetch, so the auth header is sent) navigates to it.''')\nr('''        except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n            self.send_json(e.code,''','''        except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n            if e.code == 401:\n                with LOCK:\n                    c.update(status=\"expired, reconnect\", access_token=None)\n                log(f\"{user['id']}: intervals returned 401 (revoked?) -> reconnect\")\n            self.send_json(e.code,''')\nopen('server.py','w').write(s)\na=open('static/app.js').read()\na=a.replace('<a class=\"btn\" href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\">Connect Intervals.icu</a>','<button class=\"btn\" id=\"connect\">Connect Intervals.icu</button>')\na=a.replace('    const d = document.getElementById(\"disconnect\");','''    const cb = document.getElementById(\"connect\");\n    if (cb) cb.onclick = async () => {\n      try {\n        const { authorize_url } = await api(\"/api/intervals/auth/init\", { method: \"POST\" });\n        window.location.assign(authorize_url);\n      } catch (e) { root.innerHTML = `<p class=\"card\">Error: ${esc(e.message)}</p>`; }\n    };\n    const d = document.getElementById(\"disconnect\");''')\nopen('static/app.js','w').write(a)\nc=open('config.py').read()\nc=c.replace('\"ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\"','\"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\"  # each area once; WRITE implies READ')\nopen('config.py','w').write(c)\nE\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Intervals.icu connection: causes\n\n1. **Connect button always 401s.** The button was a plain link to `GET /api/intervals/auth/init`. A page navigation doesn't send the `Authorization: Bearer` header (it's only added by the SPA's `fetch` wrapper), so the server answered `{\"error\":\"unauthorized\"}`. Fix: `auth/init` is now an authenticated `POST` returning `{authorize_url}`; the button calls it via `api()` and does `window.location.assign(...)`.\n2. **Authorize URL rejected with 400 `invalid_request`.** Since the calendar sync (2026-10-02) the scope list was `ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,...,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`. Intervals rejects a repeated area (`:WRITE` implies `:READ`) and its error body doesn't name the parameter (see `notes/`). Fix: `ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`.\n3. **\"Expired, reconnect\" after an hour.** Intervals tokens have no `refresh_token` and no `expires_in`; they live until revoked. The code assumed a default 3600s TTL, and with no refresh token the background job expired the connection. Fix: no expiry is scheduled when `expires_in` is absent. Revocation is now handled lazily: a 401 from Intervals marks the connection \"expired, reconnect\".\n\nNot verified: I couldn't test against the real Intervals.icu. The `redirect_uri` registered for the client must match `config.REDIRECT_URI`. The notes say the token exchange needs only `client_id`, `client_secret` and `code`. I left the extra `grant_type`/`redirect_uri` fields as they are, since Rivera's exchange worked with them.\nE\npython3 -c \"import ast;ast.parse(open('server.py').read())\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8099,"cache_read_input_tokens":22155,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8099},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"52780090-dd81-4a43-abcb-2dcc14dbb6bb","uuid":"9445aeee-4d85-4ed0-8c79-cded85d82c5b","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:37:19.568Z","request_id":"req_011CgENJgphT1uxskeZXThoC","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01EXo9ssLEdf8Yq6Dv2Gf1nZ":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-TycjY9; python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('server.py').read()\ndef r(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s; s=s.replace(a,b,1)\nr('''    expires_in = int(tok.get(\"expires_in\") or DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL)\n    refresh = tok.get(\"refresh_t